course: dictionary
lesson: 15286
title: One word, three jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word singing can do different jobs in a sentence. As a noun, it names an activity: «Singing is my favourite part of assembly.» Here singing is a thing you do, with words or a tune.
explain: As a verb, singing is happening now: «The choir is singing a new song.» The verb sing changes its form: sing, sings, sang, sung, singing. The -ing ending often shows that something is going on right now.
explain: As an adjective, singing describes something that makes a high, ringing sound: «The singing kettle told us the tea was ready.» To find the job, ask yourself: is it a thing, an action happening now, or a word describing something? The words around it are the clues.
fact: Singing means making musical sounds with your voice, using words or a tune.
fact: As a verb, singing shows the action is happening now, as in «She is singing.»
fact: The verb sing has the forms sings, sang and sung, so «sang» is the past.
fact: Singing can also describe a high, ringing sound, as in «singing birds».
fact: Some phrases use singing a lot: «singing lessons», «singing in the rain», «community singing» and «singing voice».
exercise: «Singing is the best part of assembly.» What kind of word is singing in this sentence? | An adjective, describing a bird | A past tense verb | A verb, happening now | *A noun, naming an activity
exercise: «The children are singing the new song.» What does singing mean here? | Sitting quietly in a circle | Clapping along to a beat | A high ringing sound like a kettle | *Making musical sounds with their voices, happening now
exercise: «The singing birds woke us at dawn.» What job does singing do in this sentence? | A noun naming a type of bird | An adjective describing the birds | A verb in the past tense | *An adjective describing the birds' high, musical calls
test: The verb sing has these forms: sing, sings, sang, sung, singing. Which one shows the action is happening now? | sung | sing | *singing | sang
test: At the birthday party we all joined in with community singing. What is singing in this sentence? | Birds calling to their mates | A kind of sports game | *A noun, making music with our voices | A high ringing sound
exam: Which sentence uses singing as an adjective? | *«The singing kettle boiled over.» | «She is singing a song in the choir.» | «We sang at the football match.» | «Singing is my favourite lesson.»
